From 62c20e99c78960c2df90ba4f87d221fdf65ad2a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:21:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 19/44] feat(chexc): clause unions, finalizer exclusions,
 pessimistic cast targets

Five conformance gaps, found by auditing the implicit-capability-passing design
rule by rule against the prototype rather than by reading it (34 probe programs):

- Several 'throws' (or 'captures') clauses on one declaration union their entries
  instead of being rejected as duplicates: generated code appends a clause rather
  than merging into an existing one, and conditional compilation emits one per
  branch. 'throws () throws A' stays an error -- the empty clause pins the list --
  and '...' repeats idempotently across the clauses of one declaration.

- Finalizers. A capability clause on '~init' is now rejected, and a finalizer is
  no longer inference-eligible: it used to acquire an inferred list and call
  checked-throwing code with no diagnostic at all, though no capability scope
  encloses a finalizer -- it may run long after the supplying handlers are gone.
  The captures scope already excluded it; inference undid that.

- Runtime casts and type patterns read functional targets pessimistically, by
  position: a function type in a covariant position receives 'throws Exception',
  one in a contravariant position keeps the empty list it spells, a parameter
  flips the polarity and a tuple keeps it. This closes a laundering hole -- 'x as
  (() -> Unit)' handed back a clause-free function whatever the value's clauses
  were, so the requirement vanished from the type system. A type argument of a
  generic is invariant and has no sound reading, so such a target is rejected;
  a clause written in a target is rejected too, since the reading decides them.
  The runtime test still uses the written type: both erase to the same shape.

- '...' is rejected on exported declarations, whose lists must not depend on
  inference.

- '()' mixed with other entries gets a dedicated diagnostic instead of the
  "expected '->' in function type" that the unit type used to produce.

Also drops the last source comments citing proposal section numbers or a notes
file: the source carries no citations, since the numbering moves.

